.alexs-rig/
# Standing memory should live in ONE place (global ~/.alexs-rig/memory or a private
# ALEXS_RIG_MEMORY repo), not be committed into each project. To keep project-local
# memory out of a repo, ignore its docs/memory/ there. This repo commits docs/memory/
# only as an example/template.
docs/memory/telemetry/
docs/memory/mining/*.jsonl
# Private, real-corpus eval sets stay local — never commit your own conversations.
evals/private/
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.venv/
.env
.env.*
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
credentials.json
id_rsa
id_rsa.pub
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
*.vsix
